# V. Investment judgement

# If only one can buy: buy a tweak

** Reason:**
The gap between the moats is decisive - the micro-letter is irreplaceable, the possum is predatory.
The gap in the quality of profits is widening — 2.5 times the net profit of the telecommunications is increasing — and the telecommunications are increasing — Ali is declining
Determining the difference - 12 times forward to the evangelical response to the probabilities of the profits, and 15 times forward to the PE to the potential recovery after two years
Free cash flow - 200 billion yuan cash flow in and out of each year. One is sending money to shareholders and one is asking for money from shareholders.

# Ali is not unbuyable, but requires higher risk tolerance

** Conditions suitable for buying Ali:**
- You believe that Ai Cloud will be Ali's core profit engine in three years.
- You can accept a 2-3-year profit period.
- You treat 574 billion dollars in cash and ant equity as a bottom line.
- You have confidence in the divisional valuation method.

# One sentence to sum up

> **Tongs like a castle that built the moat, the walls of which are still thick; Ali, like an empire that is being renovated, can't see if it's stronger or worse. The former buys certainty, the latter buys possibilities.** At the current valuation, the "determinate discount" of the evangelical is more worth buying than the "probable discount" of Ali.

